Title: Chicken Curry Recipe

Channel: indianhealthyrecipes.com

Linked recipe blog structured data (schema.org Recipe JSON-LD) — prefer this for method text when it has instructions:

{
  "@type": "Recipe",
  "name": "Chicken Curry Recipe",
  "author": {
    "@id": "https://www.indianhealthyrecipes.com/#/schema/person/2d7d264cdc5dc6602ee06a087cd3fcb0"
  },
  "description": "Simple Indian chicken curry made delicious, spicy and hot with minimum ingredients. This is a basic recipe that can be tried even by beginners. It pairs great with rice, roti or paratha.",
  "datePublished": "2014-11-10T02:00:00+00:00",
  "image": [
    "https://www.indianhealthyrecipes.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/chicken-curry-recipe.jpg",
    "https://www.indianhealthyrecipes.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/chicken-curry-recipe-500x500.jpg",
    "https://www.indianhealthyrecipes.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/chicken-curry-recipe-500x375.jpg",
    "https://www.indianhealthyrecipes.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/chicken-curry-recipe-480x270.jpg"
  ],
  "recipeYield": [
    "3",
    "3 people"
  ],
  "prepTime": "PT15M",
  "cookTime": "PT35M",
  "totalTime": "PT50M",
  "recipeIngredient": [
    "½ kg (1.1 lbs.) chicken ((preferably bone-in, boneless is okay))",
    "2 to 3 tablespoons oil",
    "1 cup (3 medium) onions ((fine chopped))",
    "1 to 2 green chilies ((slit, omit for less spicy, Thai or Indian chili peppers or serrano peppers))",
    "1 tablespoon ginger garlic paste (or ¾ inch ginger, 3 cloves garlic minced)",
    "½ cup (2 medium) tomatoes ((pureed or finely chopped))",
    "¼ cup yogurt ((or 1½ tbsp cashew butter or 12 cashews powdered &amp; pureed with ¼ cup water, refer notes))",
    "½ to ¾ teaspoon salt ((adjust as needed))",
    "½ to 1 cup hot water ((or light coconut milk))",
    "2 tablespoons coriander leaves (or mint leaves finely chopped)",
    "¼ teaspoon turmeric powder",
    "1 teaspoon Kashmiri red chili powder (or smoked paprika (½ tsp for less spicy))",
    "1 teaspoon garam masala ((½ tsp more if needed, adjust to taste))",
    "1 teaspoon coriander powder",
    "1 bay leaf (or 1 sprig curry leaves)",
    "4 cloves",
    "2 inch cinnamon piece",
    "3 green cardamom"
  ],
  "recipeInstructions": [
    {
      "@type": "HowToSection",
      "name": "Preparation",
      "itemListElement": [
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "On a medium flame, heat oil in a deep pan.  Add the whole spices - bay leaf, cinnamon, cloves &amp; green cardamoms.",
          "name": "On a medium flame, heat oil in a deep pan.  Add the whole spices - bay leaf, cinnamon, cloves &amp; green cardamoms.",
          "url": "https://www.indianhealthyrecipes.com/chicken-curry/#wprm-recipe-38246-step-0-0"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Stir in the chopped onions and chilies. Saute until deep golden in color, for 7 to 8 mins. ",
          "name": "Stir in the chopped onions and chilies. Saute until deep golden in color, for 7 to 8 mins. ",
          "url": "https://www.indianhealthyrecipes.com/chicken-curry/#wprm-recipe-38246-step-0-1"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Add ginger garlic paste and saute till you get a nice aroma, for about a minute.",
          "name": "Add ginger garlic paste and saute till you get a nice aroma, for about a minute.",
          "url": "https://www.indianhealthyrecipes.com/chicken-curry/#wprm-recipe-38246-step-0-2"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Then add tomatoes, turmeric and salt. Mix well and cook until the tomatoes turn soft &amp; mushy.",
          "name": "Then add tomatoes, turmeric and salt. Mix well and cook until the tomatoes turn soft &amp; mushy.",
          "url": "https://www.indianhealthyrecipes.com/chicken-curry/#wprm-recipe-38246-step-0-3"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Turn down the heat to low, Stir in the yogurt (or cashew paste), red chili powder, garam masala &amp; coriander powder.",
          "name": "Turn down the heat to low, Stir in the yogurt (or cashew paste), red chili powder, garam masala &amp; coriander powder.",
          "url": "https://www.indianhealthyrecipes.com/chicken-curry/#wprm-recipe-38246-step-0-4"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Cook on low heat, until the mixture smells good and aromatic.",
          "name": "Cook on low heat, until the mixture smells good and aromatic.",
          "url": "https://www.indianhealthyrecipes.com/chicken-curry/#wprm-recipe-38246-step-0-5"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Add chicken and coriander leaves. Fry on a medium heat till the chicken turns white or pale in color. This takes around 3 mins.",
          "name": "Add chicken and coriander leaves. Fry on a medium heat till the chicken turns white or pale in color. This takes around 3 mins.",
          "url": "https://www.indianhealthyrecipes.com/chicken-curry/#wprm-recipe-38246-step-0-6"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Cover and cook on a low heat for 3 to 4 minutes. This step is very important as the chicken absorbs all the flavors of the spices.",
          "name": "Cover and cook on a low heat for 3 to 4 minutes. This step is very important as the chicken absorbs all the flavors of the spices.",
          "url": "https://www.indianhealthyrecipes.com/chicken-curry/#wprm-recipe-38246-step-0-7"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Meanwhile in a separate pot, heat up 1 cup water. Using cold water most times toughens the chicken so it is good to use hot water.",
          "name": "Meanwhile in a separate pot, heat up 1 cup water. Using cold water most times toughens the chicken so it is good to use hot water.",
          "url": "https://www.indianhealthyrecipes.com/chicken-curry/#wprm-recipe-38246-step-0-8"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToSection",
      "name": "How to make Chicken Curry",
      "itemListElement": [
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Pour hot water just enough (about ½ cup) to make a thick gravy. As you cook, chicken lets out plenty of moisture, depending on that add more water. Check the pictures in the post for consistency.",
          "name": "Pour hot water just enough (about ½ cup) to make a thick gravy. As you cook, chicken lets out plenty of moisture, depending on that add more water. Check the pictures in the post for consistency.",
          "url": "https://www.indianhealthyrecipes.com/chicken-curry/#wprm-recipe-38246-step-1-0"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Cover and cook on a medium flame till the chicken is soft cooked and the curry/gravy turns thick. When the chicken is cooked completely it will fall off the bone easily. ",
          "name": "Cover and cook on a medium flame till the chicken is soft cooked and the curry/gravy turns thick. When the chicken is cooked completely it will fall off the bone easily. ",
          "url": "https://www.indianhealthyrecipes.com/chicken-curry/#wprm-recipe-38246-step-1-1"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Taste the curry &amp; add more salt if needed. You can also add another ½ tsp garam masala at this stage if you feel it is less in flavors.",
          "name": "Taste the curry &amp; add more salt if needed. You can also add another ½ tsp garam masala at this stage if you feel it is less in flavors.",
          "url": "https://www.indianhealthyrecipes.com/chicken-curry/#wprm-recipe-38246-step-1-2"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Lastly garnish with coriander leaves, cover and off the heat. Serve chicken curry with butter naan or jeera rice.",
          "name": "Lastly garnish with coriander leaves, cover and off the heat. Serve chicken curry with butter naan or jeera rice.",
          "url": "https://www.indianhealthyrecipes.com/chicken-curry/#wprm-recipe-38246-step-1-3"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
